1
00:03:39,130 --> 00:03:45,130
Could you hide a deadly secret?

2
00:07:18,260 --> 00:07:24,260
Paranoid Park is a drama, crime, mystery film directed by Gus Van Sant.

3
00:10:57,391 --> 00:11:03,391
A teenage skateboarder becomes suspected of being connected with a security guard
who suffered a brutal death in a skate park called "Paranoid Park".

4
00:14:36,521 --> 00:14:42,521
Alex, played by Gabe Nevins.

5
00:18:15,652 --> 00:18:21,652
Detective Richard Liu, played by Dan Liu.

6
00:21:54,782 --> 00:22:00,782
Jared, played by Jake Miller.

7
00:25:33,913 --> 00:25:39,913
Jennifer, played by Taylor Momsen.

8
00:29:13,043 --> 00:29:19,043
Macy, played by Lauren McKinney.

9
00:32:52,173 --> 00:32:58,173
Scratch, played by Scott Patrick Green.

10
00:36:31,304 --> 00:36:37,304
Paranoid Park is a 2007 coming-of-age teen drama film
written, directed and edited by Gus Van Sant.

11
00:40:10,434 --> 00:40:16,434
The film is based on the novel of the same name by Blake
Nelson and takes place in Portland, Oregon.

12
00:43:49,565 --> 00:43:55,565
It is the story of a teenage skateboarder (played by Gabe Nevins) set against
the backdrop of a police investigation into a mysterious death.

13
00:47:28,695 --> 00:47:34,695
Van Sant wrote the draft script in two days after
reading and deciding to adapt Nelson's novel.

14
00:51:07,826 --> 00:51:13,826
To cast the film's youths, Van Sant posted an open casting call on social networking website MySpace inviting
teenagers to audition for speaking roles, as well as experienced skateboarders to act as extras.

15
00:54:46,956 --> 00:54:52,956
Filming began in October 2006 and took place at
various locations in and around Portland.

16
00:58:26,086 --> 00:58:32,086
Scenes at the fictional Eastside Skatepark were filmed at Burnside Skatepark
which was, like Eastside, built illegally by skateboarders.

17
01:02:05,217 --> 01:02:11,217
Paranoid Park premiered on May 21, at the 2007 Cannes Film Festival
and was given a limited release on March 7, 2008.

18
01:05:44,347 --> 01:05:50,347
It grossed over US$4,481,000 from its $3 million budget.

19
01:09:23,478 --> 01:09:29,478
The film received mostly positive reviews; some critics praised the direction and cinematography in
particular, though others believed the film to be overly stylized and slow paced.

20
01:13:02,608 --> 01:13:08,608
It won one Independent Spirit Award, two Boston Society of Film Critics awards
and the Cannes Film Festival's special 60th anniversary prize.

21
01:16:41,739 --> 01:16:47,739
The film explores themes of skateboarding, portland, oregon,
trauma, male friendship, loss of virginity.

22
01:20:20,869 --> 01:20:26,869
The tone is mind_bending and dark and emotional.
